notes:
Part 1 of 3 (+ an audit card): the board command keeps the board in step with git itself, so no CLAUDE.md rule has to.

Bug it fixes (kamandsystem, 2026-11-09): board commits were pushed from temporary worktrees (the global CLAUDE.md's instruction), nothing ever fast-forwarded the project checkout, and a later `board move` there rewrote cards from a copy 19-32 commits old: Done with branch, pullRequest and comments lost (cards 6f33a3ad, 8564d0c6, aebb87c7), and once the stale copy was the truer one (78442317: Review with a merge-refused comment, while origin said Done for an open PR).

Change: every write to a git-tracked board, from the command or the screen, goes through one board sync path:
1. fetch the default branch (short timeout);
2. if the project checkout is behind and its only local changes are under .dashboard/, fast-forward it (stash-free: the board files are the only ones touched);
3. read the card fresh, apply the edit, commit to the default branch with a plain message, push;
4. a push refused because someone pushed meanwhile: fetch, re-apply, retry (bounded);
5. from a worktree (a card's or a throwaway), the same against main through a temporary worktree of origin's default branch made and removed by the command itself, so no board change ever rides in a feature branch;
6. a real clash on one card (both sides changed it): merge field by field: comments unioned by (at, body), every other field newest updatedAt wins per field; tested on 78442317's case.
Offline or no remote: write locally as today and log one warning. A board not tracked in git: unchanged.

The decisions (when to fast-forward, what to retry, the field merge) are pure modules with tests; git calls behind ports at the edge; the board files still written only through board.ts and board-store.ts (board-rule-1), through card actions (actions-rule-1). Engineering bar: clean, testable, readable, well engineered.

Afterwards, the global CLAUDE.md's 'commit it straight to the default branch ... temporary worktree' paragraph is not needed (card 3 removes it). Docs: board README, decisions, history.
